---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE_URL, SITE_NAME, CONTACT } from '../site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="WorldFreightHub's cookie policy: the cookie categories on this site, which third-party services may set cookies, their purpose and duration, and how to control them."
  canonical={`${SITE_URL}/cookie-policy/`}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Cookie Policy' }]} />
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A factual description of how this site uses cookies and similar
        technologies — which for the most part it does not. This page explains
        what is set, why, and how you control it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section container">
    <h2>1. What cookies are</h2>
    <p>
      This site, {SITE_NAME} ({SITE_URL}), is operated by YIWU DINGWEI TRADING
      COMPANY. A cookie is a small text file that a website asks your browser
      to store on your device. Cookies are commonly used to remember
      preferences, to keep a user signed in, or to measure how a site is used.
      They can be set by the site you are visiting (first-party) or by a
      service that the site loads, such as a font provider or a form service
      (third-party).
    </p>
    <p>
      "Similar technologies" — such as local storage, or the request data
      logged by a server or a third-party service — are also covered by this
      policy where they perform the same functions as cookies.
    </p>

    <h3>1.1 Types of cookie</h3>
    <p>
      Cookies are usually described in two ways: by their lifespan, and by who
      sets them.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Session cookies</strong> live only for the duration of your
        browsing session and are deleted when you close the browser. They are
        typically used for things like keeping a form submission or a login
        working while you move between pages.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Persistent cookies</strong> remain on your device for a set
        period — from minutes to years — until they expire or are deleted. They
        are typically used to remember a preference or to recognise a returning
        visitor.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>First-party cookies</strong> are set by the website shown in
        your address bar.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Third-party cookies</strong> are set by a different domain —
        for example, a font provider or a form service that a page loads.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>1.2 Local storage and similar mechanisms</h3>
    <p>
      In addition to cookies, browsers provide local storage (localStorage and
      sessionStorage), which can hold data the same way a cookie does but is
      not automatically sent with every request. This site does not use local
      storage for tracking or personalisation, and does not place any data in
      it for its own purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Cookies this site sets itself</h2>
    <p>
      This site does <strong>not</strong> set its own tracking, advertising or
      analytics cookies. We do not run analytics scripts, we do not build
      visitor profiles, and we do not require a login that would need a
      session cookie. As a result, there is no first-party cookie consent
      banner for core browsing — there is nothing of that kind to consent to.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Third-party cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Two third-party services may set or use cookies or similar storage in
      connection with this site. Both are described in the table below.
    </p>

    <h3>3.1 Cookie and technology table</h3>
    <div class="table-wrap" style="overflow-x:auto;">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Service</th>
            <th>Category</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Duration</th>
            <th>Set by</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>FormSubmit</td>
            <td>Functional / anti-abuse</td>
            <td>Processes the get-quote form and may set a session marker to
            prevent automated spam submissions.</td>
            <td>Session (ends when you close the browser)</td>
            <td>Third-party (formsubmit.co)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Google Fonts</td>
            <td>Performance / delivery</td>
            <td>Serves the Tajawal and Noto Naskh Arabic fonts used on
            Arabic-language pages; Google logs standard request data.</td>
            <td>Varies; governed by Google's own policy</td>
            <td>Third-party (fonts.googleapis.com)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>3.2 FormSubmit</h3>
    <p>
      The <a href="/get-quote/">get-quote form</a> is processed by{' '}
      <strong>FormSubmit</strong> (formsubmit.co). When you submit the form,
      FormSubmit may set a short-lived session cookie to help prevent automated
      spam. This is a functional, anti-abuse mechanism — it is not used to
      track you across other websites or to build a profile. For details of
      how FormSubmit handles data, see its own privacy documentation.
    </p>

    <h3>3.3 Google Fonts</h3>
    <p>
      The Arabic-language pages of this site load the Tajawal and Noto Naskh
      Arabic fonts from Google's font service. Google logs standard request
      data — such as the IP address, browser type and the page making the
      request — as described in Google's own privacy documentation. This only
      affects visitors to the <a href="/ar/">Arabic version</a> of the site;
      the English pages do not load Google Fonts.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Cookie categories in summary</h2>
    <p>
      For clarity, the categories of cookie that exist on this site are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Strictly necessary / functional:</strong> none set by us; a
      session marker from FormSubmit may apply only when you submit the quote
      form.</li>
      <li><strong>Performance / analytics:</strong> none. We run no analytics.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising / targeting:</strong> none. We set no advertising
      cookies and run no ad-targeting scripts.</li>
      <li><strong>Third-party delivery:</strong> Google Fonts on Arabic pages
      only, to render fonts.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Because there are no analytics or advertising cookies, there is nothing
      on this site that requires an opt-in consent banner. The only cookies in
      play are a functional anti-spam marker and a font delivery service on
      the Arabic pages.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Controlling and deleting cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Because this site sets no functional cookies of its own, no consent
      banner is required for core browsing, and clearing cookies has no effect
      on your ability to read pages or use the tools.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can control cookies in your browser settings. Most browsers let you:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>view and delete stored cookies;</li>
      <li>block third-party cookies specifically;</li>
      <li>block all cookies; and</li>
      <li>clear cookies automatically when the browser closes.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Blocking third-party cookies will disable the FormSubmit anti-spam marker
      and may stop Google Fonts from loading, but will not otherwise reduce
      this site's functionality. Consult your browser's help pages for the
      exact steps, as each browser differs.
    </p>
    <p>
      Note that some browsers offer "private" or "incognito" modes that do not
      retain cookies after the session closes. Using such a mode will not
      change your experience of this site, since there is nothing of ours to
      retain in the first place.
    </p>

    <h3>5.1 Browser-specific instructions</h3>
    <p>
      For the most common browsers, cookie controls are located as follows:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Chrome</strong> — Settings → Privacy and security → Cookies
      and other site data.</li>
      <li><strong>Firefox</strong> — Settings → Privacy &amp; Security →
      Cookies and Site Data.</li>
      <li><strong>Safari</strong> — Preferences → Privacy → Cookies and
      website data.</li>
      <li><strong>Edge</strong> — Settings → Cookies and site permissions →
      Manage and delete cookies and site data.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These locations change as browsers are updated; refer to the browser's
      own help documentation for current steps.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not engage in tracking, so it does not respond differently
      to the Do Not Track (DNT) signal — there is no tracking for DNT to
      disable. We collect no behavioural data in the first place.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Consent under GDPR and ePrivacy</h2>
    <p>
      The EU's ePrivacy Directive and the UK and EU GDPR require consent before
      placing non-essential cookies — such as analytics or advertising cookies
      — on a user's device. Because this site sets no such cookies itself, and
      its only third-party cookies are a functional anti-spam marker (FormSubmit)
      and a font delivery service (Google Fonts on Arabic pages), no consent
      banner is currently required or shown.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we ever introduce analytics, advertising or other non-essential
      cookies, we will add a consent mechanism before those cookies are placed,
      and this policy will be updated to describe them.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to this cookie policy</h2>
    <p>
      If the services this site relies on change — for example, if we add an
      analytics or advertising service in the future — this policy will be
      updated with a new "Last updated" date, and a consent banner will be
      introduced if a new category of cookie makes one necessary. We do not
      introduce tracking cookies silently, and we do not retroactively change
      the description of a cookie already described here without updating this
      page.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Relationship to the privacy policy</h2>
    <p>
      This cookie policy supplements our{' '}
      <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>, which explains what
      personal information we collect, how we use it, how long we keep it, and
      your GDPR and CCPA rights. Please read that policy for the full picture.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Cookie-related questions:{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>11. Further reading</h2>
    <p>
      The organisations below publish general, independent guidance on cookies
      and how to control them. They are listed for your convenience and are
      not affiliated with this site:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your Online Choices (EDAA)</strong> — an EU industry guide to
        behavioural advertising choices at youronlinechoices.com.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Network Advertising Initiative (NAI)</strong> — a US-based
        opt-out resource at networkadvertising.org.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>All About Cookies</strong> — general, non-technical guidance on
        cookies and how to manage them at allaboutcookies.org.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These links point to external sites over which we have no control and
      for which we are not responsible.
    </p>
    <p>
      Related policies:{' '}
      <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/terms-of-use/">Terms of Use</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 23 October 2026</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
